@inproceedings{sultani2018,
  author={Sultani, Waqas and Chen, Chen and Shah, Mubarak},
  title={Real-World Anomaly Detection in Surveillance Videos},
  booktitle={Proceedings of the IEEE/CVF Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition},
  year={2018},
  pages={6479--6488},
  doi={10.1109/CVPR.2018.00678},
  abstract={
  	Problem Statement {
  		- Annotating videos is time consuming
  		- Manual method cannot keep up with increase in cctv usage
  		- Manual method is slow and error prone
  		- Abnormal activities are rare hence harder to detect
  		- Existing models realy on feacture engineering, hence cannot generilize
  		- Some models only classify video as normla or anomaly which isn't specific
  		- Anomalous behavior is difﬁcult to deﬁne accurately
  		- In real-world anomaly activities often occur in a short portion of a video, which makes i harder to detect.
  		- Existinf datasets like UMN contioans statged videos which slightly deviated from real world videos, his can reult in miss calssifaction in production.
  		- Datasets like UCSD, Ped1, Ped2, Avenue contains videos from same locaion, which hinders model ability to generilize.
  		- Existing datasetss are staged and some anomaly videos are not realistic.
  	}
  	Proposed Method {
  		- Used weakly labeled training videos dataset i.e. the training labels (anomalous or normal) are at video-level instead of clip-level.
  		- Also proposed a new dataset of 1900 videos with total duration 128 hours, and 13 classes, availble at http://crcv.ucf.edu/projects/real-world/. Here are the classes (Abuse, Arrest, Arson, Assault, Accident, Burglary, Explosion, Fighting, Robbery, Shooting, Stealing, Shoplifting, and Vandalism.). Most dataset videos are less that 2 minutes. while logest had  more that 10 minutes.
  		- The proposed dataset videos were taken from YouTube, LiveLeak and unedited, not prank, and only CCTV vodeos. Also removed videos with unclear anomalies
  		- Used Multiple Instance Learning (MIL) framework by treating normal and anomalous surveillance videos as bags and short segments/clips of each video as instances in a bag.
  		- Used MIL ranking loss.
  		- Video (BATCH, FRAMES, CHANNELS, WIDTH, HEIGHT) -> Prerained 3D ConvNet -> Flatten -> Linear -> Anomaly Score (BATCH, 1), where each video is 240 × 320 pixels, with 16 frames @ 30fps.
		- The input of the model is a vido, and model is based on Pretrained ConvNet and output is a singular value (Anomaly Score) e.g if video has anomaly would have a score closer to 1, while normal has Anomaly score close to 0.
  	}
  	Experimental Results {
  		- Used their new dataset of 1900 videos and 13 anomaly classes, and videos from CCTV from all over the world thanks to YouTuve, and LiveLeak ensuring diversity
  		- Used 85:15 rain test split and each video is of this shape 240 × 320 pixels, 16 frames sampled at 30 fps.
  		- Model trained for over 8k epochs
  		- The metrics used for model evaluation is Receiver Operating Charecter (ROC), and Area Under Curve (AUC), and False Alarm Rate (FAR).
  		- The propose mdoel acheived 75.41\% AUC and FAR 1.9.
  		- To classify video as anoly its output anomaly score should exceed 0.5
  	}
  	Strengths {
  		- Avoid labor-intensive temporal annotations of anomalous segments in training videos by using sing deep MIL framework with weakly labeled data.
  		- No need for clip level labeled videos
  		- Proposed dataset contains mostly CCTV videos from real-world from allover the world with the help of YouTube and LiveLeak. And videos were annotated by different people to reduce nmislabeling and unclear label videos were removed.
  		Used false alaem rate as evation method as in real world anolay activites are rare to full ensure model doesn't raise dfalse almsr in thge real world.
  	}
  	Weaknesses {
  		- The model can only tell that a video contains anomaly somewhere, but we do not know where.
  		- In MIL, precise temporal locations of anomalous events in videos are unknown.
  		- The ranking loss in the hinge-loss formulation ignores the underlying temporal structure of the anomalous video, while in the real-world anomaly often occurs only for a short time.
  		- The proposed model often raised fall alrmas for vides with oclussion, e.g inserts blocking camera view
  	}
  }
}

